  @task:TASK-APP1-03
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Starting a session creates a durable session for the token's student
    When the app authenticates with lilymay's token and starts a session on the subject "english-literature"
    Then a new active session should be returned
    And the session should belong to lilymay

  # Why: The tutoring loop works over the new transport, with per-turn durability intact
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=medium] The HTTP adapter reuses the exact tutor loop the MCP adapter wires
  @task:TASK-APP1-03
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Taking a turn returns the tutor's reply and durably records the exchange
    Given lilymay has an active session started over HTTP
    When the app sends the message "What does the dagger symbolise?" to that session
    Then the tutor's reply should be returned
    And both her message and the tutor's reply should be durably recorded on the session

  # Why: "Resume where you left off" — the list drives the app's home screen
  @task:TASK-APP1-03
  @key-example
  Scenario: Listing sessions shows the student's own sessions with their activity
